{
  "requirement": "Concurrent `verify` calls on the same domain keep separate dependency\nrecords and agent conversations, even for the same source node and criterion.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The requirement has two parts. Concurrent `verify` calls on one domain must keep (1) separate dependency records and (2) separate agent conversations. Both must hold even when the calls share a source node and a criterion.\n\n**Agent conversations and dependency records: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]`**\n- The test runs two `verify_with_agent` calls concurrently with `futures::join!`. Both use `Question` on `Node(1)`.\n- `Question`'s `criterion_path` is the fixed path `[\"question\"]`. So the two calls share the source node and the criterion. They differ only in the prompt name (`alpha` or `beta`) and in whether they read the node or its successors.\n- The `ParallelConversations` provider has a `Barrier(2)`, so the two conversations really interleave. It makes these checks on every turn:\n  - the system message matches the conversation;\n  - the history length is `2 + 2*turn`;\n  - the history contains only its own contents and never the other conversation's;\n  - the last delivered page belongs to its own conversation, even though both use the same tool-call ID.\n- The test then asserts each call's output (`alpha` and `beta`) and each provider's call count (3).\n- It stores both evidence records and asserts the dependency lists exactly. Alpha's list is just `Node(1)`. Beta's list is `OutgoingEdges(Node(1), Label, …)` plus `Node(2)`. Neither trace leaks into the other.\n- A last check confirms that the stored record for the shared criterion is the last one stored (`beta`).\n\n**Dependency records for the same node and criterion: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`**\n- Two `Review` criteria run concurrently under `validation::verify`. They share the same source node and the same criterion path `behavior`, but they differ in the input nodes they read and in their revisions.\n- A barrier makes the two executions overlap, and a timeout shows they do not wait on each other.\n- The test asserts each output, and that nothing is written before `store_evidence`.\n- After storing, it asserts that the saved record's version and dependencies are wholly one execution's and not a mix of the two.\n- It also asserts 2 executions, 2 writes and 1 final record.\n\n**Other tests.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` covers distinct nodes. It is not marked for this requirement, but it is not needed.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. Both clauses (conversations and dependency traces) and the \"same node and criterion\" boundary are exercised with strong assertions, so a shared or merged trace or conversation would fail these tests. No acknowledgments or `{fixme}` references are involved.",
  "references": "a3e904046faacd0e29b7a681bc3151d22aa775c6614cef3470f5c0caaba96651",
